{{Skl|Farming}} is one of the [[Skills]] available for players to level up as they perform certain actions that give them '''Farming''' XP.

[[Roman Numerals]] are used to express its levels in-game.

Although Farming goes from levels {{Green|1–50}} (I – L) by default, there is {{Skill XP|+50 [[Farming]]}} required to reach the first level, meaning there is a "level 0", just like all other [[Skills]]. 

The [[Farming Level Cap]] can be increased through [[Jacob's Farming Contests]], to a maximum of Level 60 (LX). In order to reach this cap, players must place in the '''{{Gold|GOLD}}''' bracket of a unique crop type, then purchase the upgrade from {{NPCSprite|Anita}} in the {{Zone|Farmhouse}}. This can be done 10 times, increasing the cap one level for each unique crop type mastered.

== Mechanics ==
=== Public Islands ===
Farming on {{green|Public Islands}} serves mostly as an introduction to the skill and the means to unlock various collections. It ranges across:
**the {{Zone|Hub}} (in the {{Zone|Village}}, {{zone|Mountain}} and {{zone|Farm}} areas);
**the [[Farming Islands]] (in {{Zone|The Barn}} and {{zone|Mushroom Desert}}, on the later of which are {{Item|Glowing Mushroom}}s);
**to the {{Zone|Crimson Isle}} (featuring {{Item|Nether Wart}}s as well as the unique crops of {{Item|Mushroom Spore}}s and {{Item|Red Thornleaf}} which require {{Item|Spore Harvester}} and {{Item|Thornleaf Scythe}} respectively to be collected). 
More focused or thorough Farming is done better on the {{Zone|Garden}}, if the crops allow it.

Inside the [[Rift Dimension]] players can also find the unique crops of {{Item|Riftwart Roots}}, {{Item|Agaricus Cap}}, {{Item|Caducous Stem}}, {{Item|Half-Eaten Carrot}} and {{Item|Wilted Berberis}}, which can only be harvested using the {{Item|Wand of Farming}}. 
* Those crops cannot be planted on the Garden, but fortunately, comparatively fewer are required.

The [[Farming Islands]] also feature mobs of the {{MobType|Animal}} type, which grant {{skl|Farming|XP}} when slain, and have their own farming collections. 
* Those cannot be grinded efficiently, and as such [[Minions]] are recommended. 
* For manual grinding, [[Animal Axes]] allow the player who wishes to finish their collections manually.

=== Private Islands ===
{{Main|Garden}}
* Before the release of {{Zone|Garden}}, players would build Farms on their own {{Zone|Private Island}}, as it was significantly more efficient than Farming on {{green|Public Islands}}, whether it was for [[Collection]], {{skl|Farming|XP}} or {{c}}. 

*The addition of {{Zone|Garden}} made the building of farms much easier and farming itself much more efficient.
**Once it has been unlocked — which requires {{SkyBlock Level|5}} and is then accessed via {{NPCSprite|Sam}} who appears on player's [[Private Island]] — Farming on [[The Garden]] is the only viable way to Farm, as Public islands frequently have multiple people and don't allow for custom farms; and on [[Private Island]], player's {{stat|FmF}} is disabled. 
**Unlocking plots on it requires {{Item|Compost}}, obtained from [[Composter]] and before being able to use unlocked plots, players first need to clean them. This can be done with vanilla tools or via {{Item|Sam's Scythe}}, {{Item|Garden Scythe}} or {{Item|Plot Eraser}}.
** It offers presets for each of the crops, ready to paste.
***Despite this, players have conceived and perfected their own farm designs, seeking for {{blue|smaller space}}, {{blue|accessibility}} and the {{blue|maximum number of crops broken per second}}. 
***Players can build Farms using [[Tools]] such as the {{Item|Builder's Wand}}, the {{Item|Builder's Ruler}}, the {{Item|InfiniDirt™ Wand}}, the {{Item|Magical Water Bucket}} or the {{Item|Block Zapper}}, as well as vanilla tools enchanted with {{Ench|Efficiency}}.
* Crops, similarly to vanilla Minecraft, require {{Item|Water}} to grow, they however don't require a light source. 
**Crops each require a different [[w: Substrate (biology)|Substrate]], such as Tilled Dirt for {{Item|Wheat}} or {{Item|Carrot}}s, or {{Item|Soul Sand}} for {{Item|Nether Wart}}. 
**Dirt can be tilled en masse via {{Item|Hoe of Great Tilling}}, {{Item|Hoe of Greater Tilling}} and {{Item|Hoe of Greatest Tilling}}. 
**Crops can be planted manually or using {{Item|Basket of Seeds}} and {{Item|Nether Wart Pouch}}. {{Item|Red Mushroom|text=Red}} and {{Item|Brown Mushroom}}s however cannot be planted using these items and can only be done manually.
** The {{Ench|Replenish}} enchant, obtained from {{Coll|Cocoa Beans 8}}, automatically replants crops upon every harvest.
**The {{Ench|Delicate}} enchantment, obtained from {{NPCSprite|Anita}}, prevents the breaking of Pumpkin & Melon stems, as well as crops that are not fully grown.

==== Farming Tools ====
{{Main|Farming Tools}}
There are {{Green|12}} unique Farming Tools. 
* They can stored in the {{Item|Farming Toolkit}}, which is a Consumable purchased from [[SkyMart]] for {{Copper|500}}. Once consumed it can be accessed with:
**{{code|/FarmingToolkit}};
** by {{keypress|Shift|Right-Clicking}} a tool that has been donated to the Toolkit;
** the storage menu.
* They are crop specific and grant extra {{stat|Crop Fortune}} to their specialised [[Crop]].
* They can be leveled up to increases their stats, amount of [[Gemstone Slots]] and [[Rarity]] by:
**gaining {{Skill|Farming|XP}} while farming using the Tool;
** applying {{Item|Tool Exp Capsule}}s, these level the tool up to level {{Green|40}} by default. This limit can be increased to {{Green|50}} using a total of {{Item|Overclocker 3000|amount=10}}s.

==== Pests ====
{{Main|Pests}}
By reaching {{Garden|5}}, players unlock a new unique mechanic — Pests. 
* When farming on {{zone|Garden}}, one of {{green|13}} (one for every crop) pests may spawn. The same happens once for {{green|every real-life hour}} of {{zone|Garden}} being unloaded. 
* Up to {{Green|8}} can be spawned at the same time, and the more of them there are, the more is player's {{stat|FmF}} reduced.
* {{Item|Pest Repellent}}s slow their spawning, but it is recommended to instead kill them using [[Vacuums]], as each pest drops Crops as well as unique items which can help players farm. Additionally, by slaying Pests players obtain a special currency — {{Pests}} — which can be traded with {{NPCSprite|Phillip}} for Pest-related items.

This mechanic has been introduced to fight against scripting.

==== Greenhouse ====
{{Main|Greenhouse}}
The [[Greenhouse]] is a plot in {{Zone|Garden}}.
* It can be accessed at {{Garden|7}} ({{green|{{romnum|7}}}}) after accepting the {{NPCSprite|Carpenter}} as a [[The Garden#Visitor|Visitor]] and obtaining the {{Item|Greenhouse Blueprint}}. 
* The size of useable {{Item|Farmland}} inside the [[Greenhouse]] can be increased by using {{Item|Ethereal Vine}}s, which can be obtained when harvesting [[Mutations]] and [[Crops]] inside the [[Greenhouse]]. 
* Up to {{Green|3}} [[Greenhouse]] plots can be placed at once.
* Most of the [[Crops]] and [[Mutations]] require water while growing in the [[Greenhouse]]. 
**They can be watered with the use of a {{Item|HydroCan™ 1000}} or its upgrades. 
**If not watered, the plant has a chance to not grow, and if it reaches {{Green|0}}, die.
** The status of plants within the [[Greenhouse]] can be viewed with a {{Item|Plant Diagnostics Tool}}.

====== Mutations ======
{{Main|Mutations}}
* [[Mutations]] can be grown in the [[Greenhouse]] when [[Crops]] and other [[Mutations]] meet specific requirements within the [[Greenhouse]].

